        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>corneal</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>Compared to terrestial animals, the cornea of zebrafish is relatively flat. It consists of nonpigmented, stratified squamous nonkeratinizing epithelial cells, attached to a thick basement membrane that is considered to be analogous to the Bowman&apos;s membrane in mammals. In fish, and aquatic vertebrates in general, the cornea plays no role in focusing light, since it has virtually the same refractive index as water</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <rdfs:label>cornea</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:depicted_by rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/Schematic_diagram_of_the_human_eye_en.svg</foaf:depicted_by>
    </owl:Class>
    


