        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>lienal</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>splenic</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>In humans, it is located in the left upper quadrant of the abdomen. It removes old red blood cells and holds a reserve in case of hemorrhagic shock, especially in animals like horses (not in humans), while recycling iron</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000009>It synthesizes antibodies in its white pulp and removes, from blood and lymph node circulation, antibody-coated bacteria along with antibody-coated blood cells</obo:UBPROP_0000009>
