            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>currently this class conflates a generic layer of muscle and a specific layer found lining the digestive tract (the muscularis externa), typically composed of circular and longitudinal layers (although this varies)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000009"/>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006676"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>typically smooth muscle, but there may be exceptions - in the upper esophagus, part of the externa is skeletal muscle, rather than smooth muscle.</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <rdfs:label>muscular coat</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


