        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>note we reserve the subclass &apos;heart&apos; from the vertebrate multi-chambered heart. &apos;The first heart-like organ is believed to have appeared 500my ago in an ancestral bilaterian&apos;. Amniotes: four-chambered heart. Amphibians: two atria, one ventricle, pulmonary; fish: single atrium and ventricle; amphioxus: tubular, non-striated, closed, unidirectional; ascidians: tubular, striated, open, bidirectional; arthropods: tubular, open; C elegans: contractile pharynx; Cnideria: striated muscle cells associated with gastrodermis</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <rdfs:comment>Gene notes: Bmp, Nkx, Gata</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>primary circulatory organ</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


